Another set of ideas for new character classes:

Martial Artists:  Starts with no weapons or armor, but has a high dex and 
high con. Gets bonuses to strength for kicking as an attack and for 
breaking locks and doors. At high levels may even be able to break through 
walls, as if possessing a pick-axe, but can only do so a couple of times 
before hurting a leg. 

Olympiad:  Olypiads start with one or two intrinsics, and may gain new 
ones with level. They have good str, dex, and con. The may start with high 
speed,  built in jumping, intrinsic water walking(swimming),  increased 
kicking dammage (boxing or Karate/Tae Kwon-do), or perhapse a very high 
stat. They start with wepons like a spear (javelen) or a boomerang 
(discus). They may have some food, but they won't have much else.  

Magician/Charlitan: This person can use slight of hand for show or 
trickery. Starts with a bag of holding, a mirrror. And minor magic that 
can be highly usefull.

Aquatic/?????: fill in the blank. In D&D you can play an aquatic elf or 
half aquatic elf/ half human or half normal elf. This would be the later 
two. The character does not die in water, and may swimm in the water, if 
the character isn't incumbered to much (ie. has only a few items, or a bag 
of holding, and isn't wearing heavy armor) he or she may move around in 
the water. A heavaly loaded character find pool's to be like pits. 
 
Super-Hero: This character starts next to no possestions other than a 
tacky costume. Has very high stats, and either randomly choosen 
intrinsics, or the player gets to choose them . Atruibutes would include 
things that could normaly only be possesed by having an item (like boots 
for jumping.)  The hero might even get to use the #monster comand without 
being a monster or have built in spells that he can't loose, like 
lightning bolt.  Heroes would take  sh*t- loads of experiance to raise in 
levels, and they would only get half the points for scoring. If random 
intrinsics  were used, the character would have his origin: "A glowing 
cave spider  comes  up and bites you. A wierd transformation occurs. You 
feel strong. You feel agile. You feel  healthy. You feel alert. You feel a 
strange tingling in your head. You feel fast."
" You are no longer just Peter Parker, type in a new heroic name:"
	I think the characters should could be  choice. "Do you want to me 
to choose your intrinsics or should I?"  If the character could choose his 
intrinsics on a point based system,  with a list of point levels for built 
in spells, intrinsics, increased stats, #monster abilities?, and so on. If 
the built in spells were used, the #monster abilities would be unessisary.
	
	A few examples:
	
	Spider-Man chose
	Warning ( spider-sense. may also include ability to detect cursed items)
	Enhansed Strength,Dex*3,Con
	Increased speed
	Special item  (Web-Shooter makes web that disolves over time.)
	
	Wonder Woman chose
	Enhansed  Str,Dex,Con,
	Reflection based on special worn item (bracelets.)
	Special item magic-lasso, sleeps opponent if used correctly, works 
as leash.
	
	Batman: Enhansed, Dex, lots of special items, and potions.
	
	Long-Shot: Enhansed Dex, intinsic extra luck, good luck doesn't 
time out. The luck dissapears when he isn't stridently alligned. Has a 
bunch of little +1 darts (throwing knives). Enhansed speed.
	
	Super-Man: Only works in discovery mode. Enhased Str 18/**, Con 18
Intrincic spell magic missle (heat vision) intrinsic, levetation by 
choice, all resistances except magic. Built in armor. Etc.


	Normal hero: One or two enhansed stats. One special ability (built 
in spell or an intrinsic that can only be gained by an item.)  Two or 
three intrinsics. 
	
	
	The creations of the character could be handeled in a sub program, 
any options should be tailored to make the least number of alterations in 
the game. Heroes all start as lawfull, and they get to chose the names of 
the relevent gods.  Unless they request it durring creation, Heroes start 
with no pet. This is to counter thier power. The hero could choose a 
special pet in creation. The hero class could also be used to create your 
own new classes. In this case you would have to have a seperate progam for 
creating a class. New classed could be stored in a file that would be 
accest only if the player  typed in -New  or some such command. If  it 
could be worked in, players could post the statistics for new classes over 
the net, and describe their playability. 

That was a long one. I know that the Super-Hero is a bit of a pipe dream, 
but I thought it was worth mentioning. What do you people think? I enjoy 
the ideas for new classes that other people come up with in response.


